[76.87918, "o", "# Arrow Library - Notes for Fuzz Testing\r\n\r\n## Overview\r\nArrow is a Python library for creating, manipulating, formatting and converting dates, times and timestamps.\r\n\r\n## Key Functions for Fuzzing\r\n\r\n### 1. arrow.get() - Primary parsing function\r\n- Location: arrow/factory.py -> ArrowFactory.get()\r\n- Takes various input types: strings, timestamps, datetime objects\r\n- String parsing is the main attack surface for fuzzing\r\n- Can parse ISO 8601 formats and custom formats\r\n\r\n### 2. arrow.parser.DateTimeParser.parse()\r\n- Location: arrow/parser.py\r\n- Parses datetime strings with format patterns\r\n- Complex regex-based parsing logic\r\n\r\n### 3. arrow.Arrow.shift()\r\n- Manipulates dates with relative offsets\r\n\r\n### 4. arrow.Arrow.format()\r\n- Formats Arrow objects to strings\r\n\r\n## Fuzzing Strategy\r\n- Focus on arrow.get() with random string inputs\r\n- Test various malformed date/time strings\r\n- Test edge cases: empty strings, very long strings, special characters\r\n- Test format string parsing\r\n\r\n## Dependencies\r\n- python-da"]
[76.879224, "o", "teutil\r\n- typing_extensions (for older Python)\r\n"]
[76.879345, "o", "root@5d119885e6c8:/app# "]
[99.38866, "i", "cat > /app/black/notes_for_testing.txt << 'EOF'\n# Black Library - Notes for Fuzz Testing\n\n## Overview\nBlack is an uncompromising Python code formatter that reformats entire files in place.\n\n## Key Functions for Fuzzing\n\n### 1. black.format_str()\n- Location: src/black/__init__.py (line 1177)\n- Main entry point for formatting Python source code\n- Takes source code string and Mode object\n- Returns formatted code string\n\n### 2. black.lib2to3_parse()\n- Location: src/black/parsing.py\n- Parses Python source code into AST\n- Uses lib2to3 grammar\n\n### 3. black.parse_ast()\n- Location: src/black/parsing.py  \n- Alternative AST parsing function\n\n### 4. blib2to3 parser\n- Location: src/blib2to3/\n- Low-level Python grammar parser\n\n## Fuzzing Strategy\n- Focus on format_str() with random/malformed Python code\n- Test edge cases: syntax errors, unicode, very long lines\n- Test various Mode configurations\n- Look for crashes in the parser\n\n## Dependencies\n- click\n- mypy_extensions\n- pathspec\n- platformdirs\n- tomli (Python < 3.11)\nEO"]
[99.388834, "i", "F\n"]
[99.388849, "o", "cat > /app/black/notes_for_testing.txt << 'EOF'\r\n"]
[99.388859, "o", "> "]
[99.388955, "o", "# Black Library - Notes for Fuzz Testing\r\n"]
