[99.978836, "i", "cat > /app/ujson/notes_for_testing.txt << 'EOF'\n# UltraJSON (ujson) Library - Notes for Fuzz Testing\n\n## Overview\nUltraJSON is an ultra-fast JSON encoder and decoder written in C with Python bindings.\n\n## Key Functions for Fuzzing\n\n### 1. ujson.loads()\n- Decodes JSON string to Python object\n- Main attack surface - parsing untrusted JSON\n- C implementation - potential for memory issues\n\n### 2. ujson.dumps()\n- Encodes Python object to JSON string\n- Options: indent, ensure_ascii, encode_html_chars, escape_forward_slashes\n- Can have memory/refcount issues\n\n### 3. ujson.decode() - alias for loads()\n\n### 4. ujson.encode() - alias for dumps()\n\n## Fuzzing Strategy\n- Focus on ujson.loads() with malformed JSON strings\n- Test edge cases: deeply nested objects, large numbers, unicode\n- Test ujson.dumps() with complex Python objects\n- Look for crashes, memory leaks, refcount issues\n- Reference existing tests/fuzz.py for patterns\n\n## Dependencies\n- None (C extension module)\n- Requires compilation with setup.py\nEOF\n"]
